ment-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Critical bridge length and a polynomial polygon observable","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:cb57cb3270b474fd6660173a35a47e9a2f1003af9972f8a27188592abe530cb1","file":"preprints/Polynomial-vacuum-representations-and-bridge-mass-for-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":34,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"294f1b7ef368a37ac37b781e6a70ad996154de38c28f2fc31b5fde453ad82c1f","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Polynomial-vacuum-representations-and-bridge-mass-for-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:cb57cb3270b474fd6660173a35a47e9a2f1003af9972f8a27188592abe530cb1","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Polynomial-vacuum-representations-and-bridge-mass-for-honeycomb-walks-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L34"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:pv:bridge}\nAs the integer layer height $h$ tends to infinity,\n\\[\n b_h=h^{-1/4+o(1)},\\qquad\n \\ell_h=h^{13/12+o(1)},\\qquad\n \\mathbb E_h|\\gamma|=h^{4/3+o(1)}.\n\\]\nAll three sums are finite. These exponents are unchanged if the paths\nare also confined to horizontal distance $h\\log^2h$ from their initial\nport."}
